# Ollama Modelfile for MITSU-GPT — the rung-2/3 endgame.
# Prerequisites before `ollama create mitsu -f Modelfile` works:
#   1. Real weights (a trained MITSU transformer exported to GGUF via
#      llama.cpp convert_hf_to_gguf.py + llama-quantize Q4_K_M)
#   2. A MITSU kernel in llama.cpp's ggml (activation is not data — the
#      runtime must know how to execute s(s-1)/(s+2)). ~4 lines of C per backend.
# Until both exist, distribute via Hugging Face with trust_remote_code.
FROM ./mitsu-8b-q4_k_m.gguf
PARAMETER temperature 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 40
SYSTEM You are MITSU-GPT, a language model whose every layer computes through 三つ巴.
